2.1 "**Confidential Information**" means all information disclosed by or on behalf of Meridian to the Recipient, whether in writing, orally, electronically or by inspection, including patient and operational data, hospital performance metrics, financial information, vendor arrangements, technology systems, strategies and the existence and terms of the discussions between the parties.

2.2 Confidential Information does not include information that the Recipient can show by written records:
   (a) is or becomes public through no fault of the Recipient;
   (b) was known to the Recipient before disclosure without restriction;
   (c) is received from a third party lawfully and without restriction; or
   (d) is independently developed by the Recipient without use of the Confidential Information.
